---
export const title = 'Keyboard and accessibility';
export const order = 300;
---

<p>
  The bell is a button named "Notifications, 3 unread" (<code>label</code> replaces "Notifications"), with
  <code>aria-haspopup="dialog"</code> and <code>aria-expanded</code>; the badge on it is hidden from
  assistive technology because the button's name already carries the count.
</p>
<p>
  The panel is a non-modal dialog named by its headline. Focus moves into it when it opens and back to the
  bell when it closes; Escape, a press outside, the close button or the bell close it. Each day is a list
  labelled by its day heading, and an unread notification is read with "Unread" before its title. The All
  and Unread filters are toggle buttons (<code>aria-pressed</code>).
</p>
<p>
  When unread notifications arrive while the panel is closed, a polite live region announces them, for
  example "2 new notifications". Changes to existing notifications are not announced.
</p>
<p>
  The strings are translated with <code>setPeacockStrings()</code>: <code>notificationCenterLabel</code>,
  <code>notificationCenterBell</code>, <code>notificationCenterNew</code>,
  <code>notificationCenterFilter</code>, <code>notificationCenterAll</code>,
  <code>notificationCenterUnread</code>, <code>notificationCenterMarkAllRead</code>,
  <code>notificationCenterMarkRead</code>, <code>notificationCenterMarkUnread</code>,
  <code>notificationCenterYesterday</code>, <code>notificationCenterEmpty</code>,
  <code>notificationCenterEmptyUnread</code>, <code>notificationCenterLoadMore</code> and the shared
  <code>today</code>, <code>close</code>, <code>loading</code> and <code>dismissNotification</code>.
</p>
